antage":0.013434707862512066,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":37.8,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":0.02754875701012807,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":27.5,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.025144166240415572,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":39.0,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.10925461834653025,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.19492,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"MNTN, Inc. operates a technology platform that brings performance marketing to Connected TV. Its self-serve technology makes running TV ads as easy as search and social and helps brands to drive measurable conversions, revenue, site visits, and more. The company was formerly known as MNTN Digital, Inc. and changed its name to MNTN, Inc. in 2022. MNTN, Inc. was incorporated in 2009 and is headquartered in Austin, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Patrick A. Pohlen J.D. | Chief Financial Officer | Age 65 | Compensation: $7.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 534 people. Revenue per employee of $543K ranks in the above the sector median among Technology peers. Each employee generates $82K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $59K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 14\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["MNTN, Inc. is a small-cap technology business with a $399M market cap on $290M of annual revenue.","Returns on capital run at 13% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically. Gross margins of 77% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $44M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 15 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","Accruals are elevated at -16.6% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage runs at 7.7\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 2.5% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and stock-based comp at 11% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 19% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.4\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 7.6% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $10.3M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (35% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Antitrust and platform-regulation risk \u2014 the larger the network effect, the larger the regulatory target on its back, and a single consent decree can reset the moat.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"AI disruption of existing software moats \u2014 incumbents with durable margins face commoditisation as AI-native competitors replicate features at a fraction of the R&D cost.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 59% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 87% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Gross margin tops the Technology peer set \u2014 genuine pricing power is present here","Among the least levered in Technology \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Robbins LLP Reminds MNTN, Inc. Investors That We Are Investigating the Company for Violations of Securities Laws","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/robbins-llp-reminds-mntn-inc-investors-that-we-are-investigating-the-company-for-violations-of-securities-laws-302932230.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793994900.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.026,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["legal"]},{"title":"MNTN SHAREHOLDER INVESTIGATION: SueWallSt Notifies Investors of Potential Securities Claims Involving MNTN, Inc. (MNTN)","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/mntn-shareholder-investigation-suewallst-notifies-investors-of-potential-securities-claims-involving-mntn-inc-mntn-302932142.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793988120